# Email Configuration for Contact Form
# =====================================
# This file contains example environment variables.
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your actual values.

# SMTP Server Configuration
# --------------------------
# For Gmail: smtp.gmail.com (use App Password, not regular password)
# For SendGrid: smtp.sendgrid.net
# For Mailgun: smtp.mailgun.org
# For AWS SES: email-smtp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com (adjust region)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com

# SMTP Port
# ---------
# 587 for TLS (recommended)
# 465 for SSL
# 25 for unencrypted (not recommended)
SMTP_PORT=587

# SMTP Authentication
# -------------------
# Your SMTP username (often your email address)
SMTP_USER=your-email@gmail.com

# Your SMTP password
# For Gmail: Use an App Password (https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833)
# For other providers: Use your account password or API key
SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-password-here

# Email Addresses
# ---------------
# Where contact form submissions should be sent
CONTACT_EMAIL_TO=inferaform@gmail.com

# The "from" address that appears in emails
CONTACT_EMAIL_FROM=huzaifa@inferaform.com

# Setup Instructions
# =================
#
# 1. Gmail Setup (Recommended for testing):
#    - Enable 2-Factor Authentication on your Google account
#    - Generate an App Password: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#    - Use your Gmail address as SMTP_USER
#    - Use the 16-character App Password as SMTP_PASSWORD
#    - Set SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#    - Set SMTP_PORT=587
#
# 2. SendGrid Setup:
#    - Sign up at https://sendgrid.com
#    - Create an API Key with "Mail Send" permissions
#    - Use "apikey" as SMTP_USER
#    - Use your API key as SMTP_PASSWORD
#    - Set SMTP_HOST=smtp.sendgrid.net
#    - Set SMTP_PORT=587
#
# 3. Other SMTP Providers:
#    - Check your provider's documentation for SMTP settings
#    - Most providers support port 587 with TLS
#
# 4. Testing:
#    - After configuration, test the contact form on your website
#    - Check your email inbox (and spam folder) for test submissions
#    - Review server logs for any error messages
